Here's how to handle each scenario in MSTest:

## 1. Windows-Only Tests

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
// Or if using MSTest 3.x+:
[SupportedOSPlatform("windows")]
public void RegistryTest()
{
    // Alternatively, skip manually:
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows");

    // ... registry code
}
```

## 2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("RequiresGPU")]
public void GpuTest()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") is not null)
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI — requires local GPU");

    // ... GPU code
}
```

Filter at the command line: `dotnet test --filter "TestCategory!=RequiresGPU"`

## 3. Flaky External API — Retry

```csharp
// MSTest 3.2+ has built-in retry:
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)] // retries up to 3 times on failure
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    var result = CallWeatherApi();
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

For older MSTest without `[Retry]`, use a manual loop:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void WeatherApiTest_ManualRetry()
{
    Exception last = null;
    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
    {
        try
        {
            var result = CallWeatherApi();
            Assert.IsNotNull(result);
            return; // passed
        }
        catch (Exception ex) { last = ex; }
    }
    Assert.Fail($"Failed after 3 attempts: {last!.Message}");
}
```

## 4. Cleanup Even on Failure

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private string _tempFile = null!;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Always runs, even if the test fails or throws
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void ProcessFile()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile, "data");
        // ... test logic that might throw
    }
}
```

**Summary of key mechanisms:**

| Scenario | Approach |
|----------|----------|
| OS-specific | `Assert.Inconclusive()` / `[SupportedOSPlatform]` |
| Skip in CI | Check env var + `[TestCategory]` for filtering |
| Flaky/retry | `[Retry(N)]` (MSTest 3.2+) |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` method |
